<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56484" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλ-ευσμα</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλ-ευμα</span></b>  (v. infr.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κελεύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>order, command</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				235
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1219
			</span></i> (pl.), etc.; <i>call, summons</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				751
			</span></i> (pl.): in Prose, <i>word of command</i> in battle, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				929
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Κύριος ἐν κ. καταβήσεται ἀπ᾽
					οὐρανοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Thess.</u>
					4.16
				</span></i>
			; also, the <i>call</i> of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κελευστής</span> (q.v.), which gave the time to the rowers,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ ἑνὸς κελεύσματος</span> all at
			once, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.92
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἑνὸς κελεύματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sophr.
					25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ κελεύματος</span> at <i>the
				word of command</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				397
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1405
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καχάζετε . . ἀπὸ κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eub.
					8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατεύσονται ἀφ᾽ ἑνὸς κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Pr.</u>
					30.27
				</span></i>
			; of the boatswain's <i>pipe</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλευσμα προσαυλεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.15
				</span></i>
			 K.; also, the <i>call</i> of the driver to his horses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κελεύματι μόνον καὶ λόγῳ ἡνιοχεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					253d
				</span></i>
			; of the huntsman to his hounds, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				6.20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. κυνηγετῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ichn.</u>
					225
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέλευμα</span> is the more
			ancient form, as in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				397
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				751
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sophr.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> (codd.l.c.), <i><span class="en">
				X.
			</span></i>, ll.cc., v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> ll. cc., <i><span class="en">
				Th.
			</span></i> l. c.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
